772
00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:42.420
I mean, we've talked about this, or have we, that I do cartoons.

773
00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:43.560
I do cartooning.

774
00:30:43.680 --> 00:30:45.040
She's very good at cartooning.

775
00:30:45.140 --> 00:30:47.000
And I have a few that you've drawn that I've saved.

776
00:30:47.200 --> 00:30:48.300
I think you're fantastic.

777
00:30:48.300 --> 00:30:50.780
Well, I love my little expressive cartoons.

778
00:30:50.780 --> 00:30:54.600
But I needed Pam and wanted Pam to be a better artist than I am.

779
00:30:54.980 --> 00:30:59.040
So there is a young art student that does all of Pam's drawings.

780
00:30:59.240 --> 00:31:10.080
They went out to a bunch of people, like 12 different artists, to turn in samples to be the artist behind Pam.

781
00:31:10.240 --> 00:31:11.580
And they picked a young woman.

782
00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:14.420
Now, Jenna, I read, and you can tell me if this is true.

783
00:31:14.420 --> 00:31:26.700
I read that the first painting that they had for this episode to give to Meredith from Pam, that they had one of our set art people, who was a man, do it.

784
00:31:26.820 --> 00:31:27.000
Yeah.

785
00:31:27.160 --> 00:31:29.080
And when they looked at it, it looked too masculine.

786
00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:29.520
Yeah.

787
00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:31.840
And so then they went out to female artists.

788
00:31:32.020 --> 00:31:32.480
That's true.

789
00:31:32.700 --> 00:31:33.900
To have a little bit of a softer touch.

790
00:31:34.080 --> 00:31:34.220
Yeah.

791
00:31:34.380 --> 00:31:37.660
And there were something like 12 different artists who all submitted their work.

792
00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:39.760
And I wish I knew her name.

793
00:31:39.880 --> 00:31:40.820
Unfortunately, I don't.

794
00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:44.600
But maybe I can find that out and reveal that in a future episode.

795
00:31:44.980 --> 00:31:46.560
And then, so finally, two more gifts.

796
00:31:46.720 --> 00:31:49.440
Meredith got Dwight some shot glasses from Cancun.

797
00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:51.720
And Kevin got himself a footbath.

798
00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:57.460
Guys, around 5 minutes, 55 seconds, there is a scene where Michael is talking to Jim at Jim's desk.

799
00:31:57.520 --> 00:32:01.440
This is when he reveals that he got Ryan for Secret Santa.

800
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:05.420
And I just want to say, you see a ton of background action.

801
00:32:05.880 --> 00:32:07.700
Angela, you're walking from reception.

802
00:32:08.100 --> 00:32:10.940
Over Steve's shoulder, you see Toby and Mindy talking.

803
00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:11.400
Yeah.

804
00:32:11.920 --> 00:32:14.400
They are 100% not in character.

805
00:32:14.620 --> 00:32:16.240
Not in character at all.

806
00:32:16.420 --> 00:32:17.180
I saw that, too.

807
00:32:17.180 --> 00:32:21.460
I was like, they're just talking about probably something in the writer's room or a story pitch.

808
00:32:21.560 --> 00:32:22.780
Or they're just having a conversation.

809
00:32:23.300 --> 00:32:23.500
Yeah.

810
00:32:23.620 --> 00:32:25.420
I mean, Paul is just being Paul.

811
00:32:25.600 --> 00:32:25.720
Yeah.

812
00:32:25.840 --> 00:32:30.220
If anyone's curious, the difference between Toby and Paul, go to 5 minutes, 55 seconds.

813
00:32:30.220 --> 00:32:30.440
Yeah.

814
00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:32.740
And you can see Paul and Mindy having a conversation in the background.

815
00:32:32.840 --> 00:32:33.480
Yeah, exactly.

816
00:32:35.240 --> 00:32:36.120
Tree lighting.

817
00:32:36.580 --> 00:32:37.000
Okay.

818
00:32:37.080 --> 00:32:38.520
I've been waiting for this moment.

819
00:32:38.980 --> 00:32:40.100
The Christmas tree lighting.

820
00:32:40.900 --> 00:32:45.000
This starts the beginning of Everyone Happy, Angela Pissed.

821
00:32:46.820 --> 00:32:50.620
So, this Christmas tree, the top of it has been hacked off by Kevin.

822
00:32:50.960 --> 00:32:54.340
It is covered in so much tinsel.

823
00:32:54.540 --> 00:32:54.780
Yeah.

824
00:32:55.160 --> 00:32:56.200
So much tinsel.

825
00:32:56.440 --> 00:32:59.000
It has a smattering of just blue and red ball ornaments.

826
00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:00.940
It's just not their best effort.

827
00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:06.120
And then it has the tiniest of tiny white lights, thanks to Phyllis.

828
00:33:06.280 --> 00:33:07.920
So, Dwight makes a big deal of it.

829
00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:11.800
He, like, takes the, like, the outlet, like, the plug.

830
00:33:11.920 --> 00:33:12.560
What do you call it?

831
00:33:13.060 --> 00:33:13.780
The plug?

832
00:33:13.880 --> 00:33:14.420
The plug.

833
00:33:14.600 --> 00:33:16.080
He takes the plug from Stanley.

834
00:33:16.080 --> 00:33:17.100
He wants to plug it in.

835
00:33:17.100 --> 00:33:18.360
He's like, just like Rockefeller Center.

836
00:33:18.680 --> 00:33:22.020
And everyone gathers around and it's like, brr, brr.

837
00:33:22.400 --> 00:33:24.280
And Phyllis is like, I'm sorry.

838
00:33:24.580 --> 00:33:30.380
And at 6 minutes 38 seconds, you see my first pissed off face.

839
00:33:30.540 --> 00:33:32.060
Like, dang it, Phyllis.

840
00:33:32.060 --> 00:33:35.840
It's also one of those moments where I feel like Angela's like, I knew it.

841
00:33:35.980 --> 00:33:36.500
I knew it.

842
00:33:36.520 --> 00:33:38.940
I knew I couldn't trust her to do these lights.

843
00:33:39.140 --> 00:33:41.220
Why do I even have her do anything?

844
00:33:41.260 --> 00:33:42.720
Why do you have anyone do anything?

845
00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:43.040
Yeah.

846
00:33:43.580 --> 00:33:45.560
You can't let anyone do anything.

847
00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:46.700
These people are worthless.

848
00:33:46.980 --> 00:33:47.340
Exactly.

849
00:33:48.160 --> 00:33:52.700
You know, that Christmas tree light thing is based on a real thing from Mike Schur's life.

850
00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:53.740
I know.

851
00:33:55.100 --> 00:34:01.120
He said that when he and his wife got their first tree in New York, he bought a bunch of small lights for the tree.

852
00:34:01.120 --> 00:34:02.200
And he wrapped them around.

853
00:34:02.360 --> 00:34:04.220
And when he plugged it in, you couldn't really see them.

854
00:34:05.960 --> 00:34:06.960
I love that.

855
00:34:07.100 --> 00:34:10.740
I love when writers work those little moments from their real life into the show.

856
00:34:11.020 --> 00:34:15.040
I thought, speaking about people who are acting like themselves instead of their characters,

857
00:34:15.260 --> 00:34:18.820
I thought Jim's talking head about Creed's gift is so John.

858
00:34:19.140 --> 00:34:19.880
It is John.

859
00:34:20.100 --> 00:34:21.560
That is John right there.

860
00:34:21.680 --> 00:34:21.860
Yeah.

861
00:34:22.160 --> 00:34:25.560
All the delivery, the smile, all of it.

862
00:34:25.800 --> 00:34:28.540
And then, of course, Creed's talking head made me laugh so hard.

863
00:34:28.800 --> 00:34:30.860
Creed is very funny in this episode.

864
00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:36.080
I mean, everybody has some great moments, but Creed cracked me up a bunch in this episode.

865
00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:38.020
So now Secret Santa is starting.

866
00:34:38.260 --> 00:34:38.440
Yep.

867
00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:41.460
And everyone is gathered around in some office chairs.

868
00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:45.320
And I want to say, truly, I know we were joking about Charles McDougal,

869
00:34:45.520 --> 00:34:53.660
but the amount of energy and movement that he uses the camera to give this scene of people sitting in a circle,

870
00:34:53.660 --> 00:34:56.820
I mean, it is impressive from a directorial standpoint.

871
00:34:56.820 --> 00:35:05.600
I think, like, I don't want to be crazy, but I think, like, film students should study this portion of the episode

872
00:35:05.600 --> 00:35:11.380
because I'm imagining myself trying to film a group of people sitting in a circle doing a gift exchange,

873
00:35:11.380 --> 00:35:13.340
and it would not look nearly this dynamic.

874
00:35:13.560 --> 00:35:15.120
It's really, really impressive directing.

875
00:35:15.400 --> 00:35:16.320
No, he's great.

876
00:35:16.440 --> 00:35:17.380
He is really great.

877
00:35:17.380 --> 00:35:21.360
Okay, so we're starting the Secret Santa, and Pam opens Jim's teapot.

878
00:35:21.560 --> 00:35:26.140
She loves it, but Dwight moves things along so quickly that she doesn't have time to look inside

879
00:35:26.140 --> 00:35:27.900
or notice the card that's in the box.

880
00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:29.860
Yeah, Dwight wants no chitty chat between gifts.

881
00:35:29.980 --> 00:35:30.860
He's like, go, go, go, go, go.

882
00:35:30.860 --> 00:35:32.180
He's me coming in today.

883
00:35:32.300 --> 00:35:32.760
He is.

884
00:35:32.760 --> 00:35:34.220
He's like, save it for the mic.

885
00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:38.340
So he's moving things along, so it's Pam, and then the next one.

886
00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:45.060
We find out that Michael buys Ryan a video iPod that costs $400.

887
00:35:45.740 --> 00:35:47.720
You guys, this was not product placement.

888
00:35:47.960 --> 00:35:48.540
It was not.

889
00:35:48.540 --> 00:35:50.340
So many people wanted to know.

890
00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:52.180
Yeah, we were not paid.

891
00:35:52.180 --> 00:35:55.380
It was just sort of a really cool topical gift at the time.

892
00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:55.700
Yeah.

893
00:35:55.700 --> 00:36:02.880
And they were trying to think of a gift that would sort of be a showstopper that Michael would think was very impressive that everyone would want.

894
00:36:03.340 --> 00:36:04.460
So this was coincidence.

895
00:36:04.460 --> 00:36:05.800
We weren't paid to use it.

896
00:36:05.940 --> 00:36:06.960
So I read that.

897
00:36:07.980 --> 00:36:09.140
Well, here's something.

898
00:36:09.400 --> 00:36:12.460
A ton of people wanted to know who kept it at the end.

899
00:36:12.580 --> 00:36:12.840
Nobody.

900
00:36:13.100 --> 00:36:14.720
We weren't allowed to keep any of the stuff.

901
00:36:14.940 --> 00:36:23.780
It all goes into a giant warehouse, and it gets labeled for the episode for props because if for some reason we have to go back and reshoot something,

902
00:36:23.780 --> 00:36:25.880
they take it off the shelf and they bring it back in.

903
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:26.520
That's true.

904
00:36:26.660 --> 00:36:31.380
I don't know what happens after it's been in the warehouse for a while, but it just goes to prop house storage.

905
00:36:31.800 --> 00:36:35.380
I feel like it's still in a box labeled the office Christmas party.

906
00:36:35.540 --> 00:36:36.360
It probably is.

907
00:36:36.480 --> 00:36:38.880
There was a fan question from Beard Up, Beard Down.

908
00:36:39.060 --> 00:36:40.780
Was the iPod sponsored by Apple?

909
00:36:40.920 --> 00:36:41.620
It wasn't.

910
00:36:41.700 --> 00:36:42.780
We said it was not.

911
00:36:42.960 --> 00:36:44.180
It's just a total coincidence.

912
00:36:44.460 --> 00:36:46.080
But there's more coincidence.

913
00:36:47.240 --> 00:36:56.480
So the week after this episode aired, Apple revealed that you could now download episodes of The Office onto these video iPods.

914
00:36:56.660 --> 00:36:58.580
Again, this was not planned.

915
00:36:58.860 --> 00:37:04.480
And then The Office became the number one downloaded show on iTunes.

916
00:37:04.840 --> 00:37:05.360
Yes.

917
00:37:05.620 --> 00:37:07.260
The number one downloaded show.

918
00:37:07.480 --> 00:37:11.600
I remember Rainn Wilson turned to me and said, I think we're going to make it.

919
00:37:11.600 --> 00:37:17.740
But I think we're going to – this was the first moment it felt like the tide was turning for us and that we might not get canceled.

920
00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:18.420
All right.

921
00:37:18.520 --> 00:37:24.580
So next up, Michael gets his gift, the oven mitt knitted by Phyllis.

922
00:37:24.820 --> 00:37:25.160
Oof.

923
00:37:25.620 --> 00:37:27.980
Now, everyone had a $20 limit, you guys.

924
00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:32.040
That's why this iPod really shakes everything up because he spent $400.

925
00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:32.840
Yes.

926
00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:33.580
Yes.

927
00:37:34.080 --> 00:37:39.800
And he has his line where he says, I only – he says out in the hallway, he's holding the mitt.

928
00:37:39.800 --> 00:37:41.360
And he says, do you know what this says?

929
00:37:41.540 --> 00:37:45.120
This says, I only care about you, a homemade oven mitt's worth.

930
00:37:45.300 --> 00:37:46.400
He is such a child.

931
00:37:46.720 --> 00:37:49.100
He is such a bratty kid in this episode.

932
00:37:49.300 --> 00:37:49.900
Oh, my gosh.

933
00:37:49.960 --> 00:37:56.820
Well, we had a fan question from Chelsea, Raconza, and Amanda, and many others, actually, who actually knitted the oven mitt.

934
00:37:57.200 --> 00:37:58.540
Well, I asked Phyllis.

935
00:37:58.920 --> 00:38:00.540
She does not knit in real life.

936
00:38:00.860 --> 00:38:04.360
Although she told me that she knitted a scarf for her mom a couple of years ago.

937
00:38:04.400 --> 00:38:05.380
But she said that's it.

938
00:38:05.500 --> 00:38:06.760
She didn't – just one scarf.

939
00:38:06.760 --> 00:38:11.260
I want you guys to know, you know how we talk about what was at everyone's desks?

940
00:38:11.440 --> 00:38:20.680
So at Phyllis' desk, like sitting on the floor sort of next to her desk for so many years, was a whole knitting basket.

941
00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:21.500
Do you remember?

942
00:38:21.720 --> 00:38:21.980
I do remember that.

943
00:38:21.980 --> 00:38:27.760
It had all the yarn and the knitting needles, and it sat there as if her character would ever do anything with it.

944
00:38:27.860 --> 00:38:29.720
But it was established there, and it sat there.

945
00:38:29.720 --> 00:38:36.780
Well, Phil Shea told me he found a woman at a knitting store in Valley Village, California, and she knitted the oven mitt.

946
00:38:38.240 --> 00:38:45.520
Again, oven mitt knitter, if you're listening, please write us at officeladiesatierwolf.com, and we'll give you a shout-out.

947
00:38:45.720 --> 00:38:45.940
Yeah.

948
00:38:46.160 --> 00:38:47.360
You knitted the famous mitt.

949
00:38:47.560 --> 00:38:50.740
I thought it looked like a great oven mitt, and it had like the little –

950
00:38:50.740 --> 00:38:52.480
Like the Teflon.

951
00:38:52.480 --> 00:38:53.780
Teflon-y thingy on the one side.

952
00:38:53.960 --> 00:38:54.100
Yeah.

953
00:38:54.600 --> 00:39:01.120
So Ryan gets the iPod, and at 8 minutes, 24 seconds is the next phase of Angela pissed-offness.

954
00:39:01.340 --> 00:39:01.600
Okay.

955
00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:08.280
You see my face at the fact that Michael spent $400 when the limit was $20.

956
00:39:08.560 --> 00:39:09.900
All of my instructions.

957
00:39:09.960 --> 00:39:14.260
I'm sure I sent out an email about Secret Santa and the rules.

958
00:39:14.260 --> 00:39:19.240
So one, Phyllis has ignored my request for bigger lights and got the tiny lights.

959
00:39:19.380 --> 00:39:24.780
Now two, Michael has spent $400 instead of the agreed-up $20.

960
00:39:25.300 --> 00:39:26.840
So we're ramping up.

961
00:39:26.960 --> 00:39:28.280
She's getting ticked off.

962
00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:34.820
I have no doubt that you sent a very detailed email about this to everyone with a follow-up reminder.

963
00:39:35.260 --> 00:39:35.580
Mm-hmm.

964
00:39:36.220 --> 00:39:40.860
Which is why Kevin does not come forward when he gets himself, because he would have had to tell me.

965
00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:41.560
He would have.

966
00:39:41.700 --> 00:39:41.920
Mm-hmm.

967
00:39:42.020 --> 00:39:42.260
Yeah.

968
00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:43.220
You know what?

969
00:39:44.580 --> 00:39:47.820
I really relate to Angela on so many levels.

970
00:39:48.360 --> 00:39:49.140
Really do.

971
00:39:49.420 --> 00:39:52.200
There's on some levels, you're way more Angela than I am.

972
00:39:52.360 --> 00:39:52.740
Oh, yeah.

973
00:39:52.920 --> 00:39:58.860
I mean, I would have generated two, three, four very detailed emails about the party, the plans.

974
00:39:59.140 --> 00:39:59.560
Mm-hmm.

975
00:39:59.960 --> 00:40:08.000
If I assigned someone to do lights for the tree, and that's what I got, I would feel so pissed and let down.

976
00:40:08.220 --> 00:40:12.260
If people went over the $20 budget, you would have been furious.

977
00:40:12.440 --> 00:40:12.780
Furious.

978
00:40:12.780 --> 00:40:14.140
Because you would have been like, what's the point?

979
00:40:14.520 --> 00:40:16.140
Why even have that number?

980
00:40:16.300 --> 00:40:17.260
Is Angela wrong?

981
00:40:17.520 --> 00:40:18.000
No.

982
00:40:18.240 --> 00:40:19.440
I don't think she's wrong.

983
00:40:19.680 --> 00:40:24.120
She's just, you know, why is no one helping her?

984
00:40:24.120 --> 00:40:26.060
She's a by-the-book person.

985
00:40:26.200 --> 00:40:26.380
She is.

986
00:40:26.380 --> 00:40:27.920
Why can't people follow the rules?

987
00:40:27.980 --> 00:40:28.500
I agree.

988
00:40:28.980 --> 00:40:40.380
So at nine minutes, 39 seconds, she gets pissed off on a whole new level, because as you were saying, this is when Michael is really ticked off that he got the oven mitt,

989
00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:41.980
and he switches the party.

990
00:40:41.980 --> 00:40:43.340
No more Secret Santa.

991
00:40:43.560 --> 00:40:45.060
He says, now we're doing Yankee Swap.

992
00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:45.660
Yes.

993
00:40:45.940 --> 00:40:49.680
Yankee Swap slash White Elephant slash, what was the other one he said?

994
00:40:50.020 --> 00:40:50.660
Nasty Christmas.

995
00:40:51.080 --> 00:40:51.580
Nasty Christmas.

996
00:40:51.920 --> 00:40:55.140
You know, there was actually a little debate about, what do you call it?

997
00:40:55.220 --> 00:40:57.180
And people were like, well, we call it White Elephant.

998
00:40:57.260 --> 00:40:58.640
And someone else was like, we call it Yankee Swap.

999
00:40:58.740 --> 00:41:01.240
And I feel like the writers took that and put it in the episode.

1000
00:41:01.240 --> 00:41:03.600
Yeah, I know it as Yankee Swap.

1001
00:41:03.980 --> 00:41:04.740
What do you know it as?

1002
00:41:04.740 --> 00:41:05.540
I knew it as White Elephant.

1003
00:41:05.640 --> 00:41:05.840
Yeah.

1004
00:41:06.100 --> 00:41:07.400
I think it's good they did that.

1005
00:41:07.640 --> 00:41:07.900
I do, too.

1006
00:41:07.900 --> 00:41:08.660
They covered everybody.

1007
00:41:08.720 --> 00:41:09.300
They covered everybody.

1008
00:41:09.300 --> 00:41:15.300
But when I threw my Christmas party, I called it Yankee Swap, just because I loved it so much.

1009
00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:19.840
You know, here's something that I heard in the commentary, Angela, since we're talking about your character.

1010
00:41:19.840 --> 00:41:23.100
I guess that you had a talking head in the fire.

1011
00:41:23.340 --> 00:41:25.920
I watched it, because I have a DVD player now.

1012
00:41:26.020 --> 00:41:26.840
Where you cried.

1013
00:41:27.100 --> 00:41:28.400
Yes, in the deleted scenes.

1014
00:41:28.400 --> 00:41:38.340
Well, Mike said that the writers' room was so impressed with your performance and that talking head that they put a card on the wall that was Angela cries.

1015
00:41:38.360 --> 00:41:41.920
And they wanted to find an episode where you could cry a bunch.

1016
00:41:42.040 --> 00:41:42.740
And this was it.

1017
00:41:43.140 --> 00:41:47.040
Mike sure told me, he said, I love to see your character cry.

1018
00:41:47.820 --> 00:41:54.740
He said she's so pulled together that when you sort of fall apart, it's like really sort of oddly pleasing.

1019
00:41:55.420 --> 00:41:58.510
I love it.

1020
00:41:58.510 --> 00:42:01.870
So, yes, at 9 minutes 51 seconds, I have a talking head.

1021
00:42:01.870 --> 00:42:07.210
And my character is really upset, because she feels like Michael should have talked to the PPC firSt.

1022
00:42:07.470 --> 00:42:07.670
Yeah.

1023
00:42:07.830 --> 00:42:08.610
Well, they should have.

1024
00:42:08.910 --> 00:42:10.050
I mean, he should have.

1025
00:42:10.150 --> 00:42:11.530
And then she breaks down.

1026
00:42:11.730 --> 00:42:14.210
So she is really starting to spiral.

1027
00:42:14.230 --> 00:42:16.850
And then when we cut back to the scene, she's still sobbing.

1028
00:42:16.950 --> 00:42:18.730
I mean, she's not sobbing, but she's still crying.

1029
00:42:18.810 --> 00:42:19.430
She's sullen.

1030
00:42:19.610 --> 00:42:20.550
She's very sullen.

1031
00:42:20.550 --> 00:42:24.170
Okay, you know this famous line, Yankee Swap.

1032
00:42:24.330 --> 00:42:24.610
Yeah.

1033
00:42:24.930 --> 00:42:25.510
From Michael.

1034
00:42:25.770 --> 00:42:25.950
Mm-hmm.

1035
00:42:26.190 --> 00:42:26.630
All right.

1036
00:42:26.890 --> 00:42:27.670
Mike sure.

1037
00:42:28.210 --> 00:42:29.270
That's a written line.

1038
00:42:29.270 --> 00:42:30.390
That wasn't improvised.

1039
00:42:30.470 --> 00:42:32.210
That Steve would say Yankee Swap.

1040
00:42:32.350 --> 00:42:37.270
And Mike wrote in the script, in parentheses, crazy voice.

1041
00:42:38.290 --> 00:42:41.490
And he was like, I know Steve will do something great with that.

1042
00:42:41.750 --> 00:42:43.750
And that was Steve's take on that.

1043
00:42:43.910 --> 00:42:44.630
Because they would do that.

1044
00:42:44.750 --> 00:42:49.470
They would sometimes put little pieces of direction in the script for us, and then we'd have to interpret it.

1045
00:42:49.650 --> 00:42:49.830
Yeah.

1046
00:42:50.310 --> 00:42:53.810
Guys, did you notice in this episode, it is snowing outside.

1047
00:42:54.230 --> 00:42:55.630
I loved this touch.

1048
00:42:55.630 --> 00:42:59.250
I loved that they kept cutting to the windows, and there'd be snow.

1049
00:42:59.570 --> 00:43:01.710
Do you remember how much fun it was to have the snow?

1050
00:43:01.890 --> 00:43:04.190
We were so tickled by the snow.

1051
00:43:04.230 --> 00:43:04.870
We were so excited.

1052
00:43:05.010 --> 00:43:09.850
You guys remember, we mostly just filmed inside, and we never even saw outside or what was happening outside.

1053
00:43:10.150 --> 00:43:10.310
Yeah.

1054
00:43:10.410 --> 00:43:13.830
And so the fact that we had this extra element happening was so fun.

1055
00:43:13.990 --> 00:43:17.650
We really did film inside in a windowless warehouse.

1056
00:43:18.030 --> 00:43:19.670
All the windows were fake.

1057
00:43:19.890 --> 00:43:21.570
They just had backdrops behind them.

1058
00:43:21.790 --> 00:43:21.890
Yeah.

1059
00:43:21.890 --> 00:43:25.710
So to see actual sunshine or snow or air was really exciting to us.

1060
00:43:25.850 --> 00:43:27.730
I have a ton of facts about the snow.

1061
00:43:27.910 --> 00:43:34.210
I don't know if anyone else will find it interesting, but I had written all about it in one of my blogs slash journals.

1062
00:43:34.510 --> 00:43:35.670
I'm living for this.

1063
00:43:35.750 --> 00:43:37.110
I can't wait to hear about it.

1064
00:43:37.250 --> 00:43:37.410
All right.

1065
00:43:37.410 --> 00:43:38.190
I do have to pee.

1066
00:43:39.050 --> 00:43:42.730
Oh, do you want me to give you some snow facts when we come back from the break?

1067
00:43:43.030 --> 00:43:43.730
I mean, can I go pee?

1068
00:43:43.730 --> 00:43:47.110
You should be on an empty bladder when I lay these awesome facts on you.

1069
00:43:47.310 --> 00:43:50.030
You don't tell me or my bladder what we're doing.

1070
00:43:50.210 --> 00:43:50.930
Well, what do you want?

1071
00:43:50.930 --> 00:43:54.530
Do you want full bladder snow facts or empty bladder snow facts?

1072
00:43:54.550 --> 00:43:55.930
I want empty bladder snow facts.

1073
00:43:55.930 --> 00:43:56.250
All right.

1074
00:43:56.350 --> 00:43:57.210
That's what I'm saying.

1075
00:43:57.210 --> 00:44:01.210
Oh, I thought you were telling me that I had to not drink any more water or tea.

1076
00:44:01.710 --> 00:44:05.210
When we go on a road trip, my husband will be like, can you not get an iced tea?

1077
00:44:06.110 --> 00:44:06.510
Okay.

1078
00:44:06.690 --> 00:44:14.690
Clearly, you're projecting some other thing on me because I said I thought you should empty your bladder for the snow facts she's leaving.

1079
00:44:14.950 --> 00:44:17.510
First, you push away from the mic to eat your snack.

1080
00:44:17.830 --> 00:44:18.950
This is for you, Jenna.

1081
00:44:21.540 --> 00:44:22.420
It's so disgusting.

1082
00:44:22.420 --> 00:44:23.800
Those are high nut Cheerios.

1083
00:44:24.580 --> 00:44:25.400
Oh, God.

1084
00:44:31.750 --> 00:44:35.990
For letting me have my bathroom break, I want to hear all about your snow.

1085
00:44:36.250 --> 00:44:36.710
All right.

1086
00:44:36.710 --> 00:44:38.950
I hope this isn't anticlimactic for people.

1087
00:44:38.950 --> 00:44:43.650
But the company that came to make the snow is called Snow Business.

1088
00:44:44.010 --> 00:44:45.630
I love that.

1089
00:44:45.890 --> 00:44:46.590
Snow business.

1090
00:44:46.810 --> 00:44:47.590
Snow business.

1091
00:44:47.590 --> 00:44:48.390
I remembered.

1092
00:44:48.690 --> 00:44:49.850
I remembered that.

1093
00:44:50.090 --> 00:44:51.130
It so tickled me.

1094
00:44:51.490 --> 00:44:51.690
Okay.

1095
00:44:51.690 --> 00:44:54.010
So here's how it works with fake snow.

1096
00:44:54.330 --> 00:44:56.290
There's a guy from Snow Business.

1097
00:44:56.610 --> 00:44:57.430
He shows up.

1098
00:44:57.430 --> 00:45:03.530
Now, the snow that falls from the sky is different from the ground cover snow.

1099
00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:05.750
The snow on the ground is snow.

1100
00:45:05.990 --> 00:45:11.390
The snow that falls from the sky, I know, because it falls on my character at the end.

1101
00:45:11.390 --> 00:45:13.090
And it is not snow.

1102
00:45:13.270 --> 00:45:14.150
It's not snow.

1103
00:45:14.290 --> 00:45:15.030
It's soap.

1104
00:45:15.330 --> 00:45:15.810
Yes.

1105
00:45:16.030 --> 00:45:17.210
You can get a choice.

1106
00:45:17.430 --> 00:45:21.410
You can get a choice of cornstarch, plastic, or soap.

1107
00:45:21.930 --> 00:45:25.650
And Greg watched a demonstration of all three, and he picked soap.

1108
00:45:25.650 --> 00:45:32.530
Well, when by accident, a little piece of that might get in your mouth, it tastes like soap.

1109
00:45:32.750 --> 00:45:35.550
Because I shriek, and a piece of it went in my mouth.

1110
00:45:36.690 --> 00:45:38.430
That's what she said.

1111
00:45:38.930 --> 00:45:39.050
Yeah.

1112
00:45:39.410 --> 00:45:39.810
Okay.

1113
00:45:40.150 --> 00:45:42.210
On the ground, though, it's real snow.

1114
00:45:42.530 --> 00:45:44.030
And they bring this machine.

1115
00:45:44.030 --> 00:45:50.110
And I don't know exactly how it works, but it's kind of like a wood chipper, but in reverse.

1116
00:45:50.250 --> 00:45:52.370
It looks like something out of a Dr. Seuss.

1117
00:45:52.650 --> 00:45:53.510
It does.

1118
00:45:53.730 --> 00:45:54.810
It really does.

1119
00:45:54.810 --> 00:45:57.450
And it really blows snow.

1120
00:45:57.730 --> 00:45:59.030
I guess that's what it looks like.

1121
00:45:59.090 --> 00:46:01.590
It looks like a snowblower, but it generates snow.

1122
00:46:01.830 --> 00:46:06.190
And then it just blows it all over the ground, all over the cars, and all that stuff.

1123
00:46:06.410 --> 00:46:11.970
But guys, remember, this is like, we're shooting this in like October in Los Angeles.

1124
00:46:12.350 --> 00:46:14.070
And it's hot in October.

1125
00:46:14.330 --> 00:46:15.790
It stays warm here.

1126
00:46:16.090 --> 00:46:19.250
In the daytime, it's still in the mid-80s, 90s.

1127
00:46:19.830 --> 00:46:23.670
But it was night, and so we had a little bit of time with it.

1128
00:46:23.670 --> 00:46:25.590
I mean, it was still warm out.

1129
00:46:25.750 --> 00:46:26.070
Yeah.

1130
00:46:26.070 --> 00:46:28.350
It was probably like in the high 60s.

1131
00:46:28.470 --> 00:46:28.770
Yeah.

1132
00:46:29.050 --> 00:46:30.150
That sounds about right.

1133
00:46:30.470 --> 00:46:30.690
All right.

1134
00:46:30.690 --> 00:46:31.010
Yes.

1135
00:46:31.010 --> 00:46:32.710
We were very excited to have snow.

1136
00:46:33.670 --> 00:46:35.070
And Jenna, we're...

1137
00:46:35.070 --> 00:46:36.270
Did you like my snow facts?

1138
00:46:36.590 --> 00:46:40.270
I feel a little vulnerable about them now because we set them up so much.

1139
00:46:40.350 --> 00:46:42.110
I mean, there was like a break and...

1140
00:46:42.110 --> 00:46:42.490
No.

1141
00:46:42.690 --> 00:46:43.670
...in my head about it.

1142
00:46:43.670 --> 00:46:45.090
I like your snow facts.

1143
00:46:45.290 --> 00:46:45.950
Snow business.

1144
00:46:46.250 --> 00:46:47.150
That's cute.

1145
00:46:47.390 --> 00:46:49.250
I think snow business is really cute.

1146
00:46:49.450 --> 00:46:49.810
All right.

1147
00:46:49.990 --> 00:46:52.890
But let's go back to the gift exchange.

1148
00:46:53.390 --> 00:46:56.350
This is when Kelly gets Angela's poster.

1149
00:46:57.090 --> 00:46:59.470
But Angela, you do get to take it back.

1150
00:46:59.750 --> 00:47:00.170
Okay.

1151
00:47:00.190 --> 00:47:01.010
Here's the thing.

1152
00:47:01.010 --> 00:47:08.190
I wrote in my MySpace blog about this moment, and I wrote that it was one of the hardest

1153
00:47:08.190 --> 00:47:15.530
things for us to get through as a cast, that the first time Mindy unrolls the poster and

1154
00:47:15.530 --> 00:47:17.610
looks at it, and we all see it.

1155
00:47:17.810 --> 00:47:20.870
We all, every person lost it.

1156
00:47:20.930 --> 00:47:22.490
Because it's so ridiculous.

1157
00:47:22.490 --> 00:47:23.350
It's so ridiculous.

1158
00:47:23.350 --> 00:47:24.810
We had not seen it.

1159
00:47:24.810 --> 00:47:31.110
It was an actual surprise to us while we were filming, and we all lost it.

1160
00:47:31.350 --> 00:47:37.550
I had that, in fact, it was particularly hard on Rain for some reason, and that in one

1161
00:47:37.550 --> 00:47:41.350
take, he broke three times because he could not get through it.

1162
00:47:41.510 --> 00:47:47.250
I can't believe that Mindy was tasked with having to unroll that poster.

1163
00:47:47.550 --> 00:47:50.270
How did we ever get a shot of her not laughing?

1164
00:47:50.470 --> 00:47:53.110
I don't know, but we were cracking up.

1165
00:47:53.110 --> 00:47:56.850
There's a little detail in that scene that made me laugh when I rewatched it, which is

1166
00:47:56.850 --> 00:48:02.190
how you just very subtly swat the oven mitt away on your way to getting the poster.

1167
00:48:02.430 --> 00:48:03.170
That was all me.

1168
00:48:03.350 --> 00:48:04.270
Thank you very much.

1169
00:48:04.290 --> 00:48:05.850
I loved it.

1170
00:48:06.070 --> 00:48:07.510
It was such a good detail.

1171
00:48:07.750 --> 00:48:08.490
I loved it.

1172
00:48:10.690 --> 00:48:16.150
Well, in tracking the oven mitt, Meredith eventually takes the oven mitt.

1173
00:48:17.250 --> 00:48:22.930
But, you know, Michael has to then call her a sucker and say that he wanted her to take

1174
00:48:22.930 --> 00:48:26.030
it, and it was reverse psychology when he said he wanted to keep it.

1175
00:48:26.150 --> 00:48:30.630
I love that he decided that he needed to break down reverse psychology to all of us, because

1176
00:48:30.630 --> 00:48:31.730
I don't know if you've heard of it.

1177
00:48:31.850 --> 00:48:33.150
It's a pretty cool thing.

1178
00:48:33.450 --> 00:48:35.430
I'm like, Michael, you're such an idiot.

1179
00:48:35.670 --> 00:48:40.510
Do you remember how Phyllis cried during that scene?

1180
00:48:40.770 --> 00:48:43.770
Yeah, she stayed in, like, sort of that sad place.

1181
00:48:43.770 --> 00:48:49.290
She cried for, like, a half hour, and in between takes of that, where she had to be crying,

1182
00:48:49.430 --> 00:48:50.810
she didn't want any of us to talk to her.

1183
00:48:50.870 --> 00:48:52.750
And Kate and I tried to go up and give her a hug.

1184
00:48:53.010 --> 00:48:54.150
She didn't want it.

1185
00:48:54.230 --> 00:48:56.090
Like, she was in this, like, actor zone.

1186
00:48:56.270 --> 00:48:58.010
It's so hard to do.

1187
00:48:58.430 --> 00:48:59.670
It's so hard to do.

1188
00:48:59.810 --> 00:49:03.410
I know exactly where she was, but I just remember being really worried for her, because

1189
00:49:03.410 --> 00:49:08.010
when you see Phyllis cry, it is, ugh.

1190
00:49:08.410 --> 00:49:09.830
You don't want to see Phyllis cry.

1191
00:49:09.950 --> 00:49:10.930
You don't want to see her cry.

1192
00:49:10.930 --> 00:49:12.370
Because it breaks every part of you open.

1193
00:49:12.370 --> 00:49:14.150
I mean, she did.

1194
00:49:14.270 --> 00:49:15.790
She had to stay sad.

1195
00:49:15.790 --> 00:49:22.230
And it is really hard, especially sitting in this circle with people cracking up about

1196
00:49:22.230 --> 00:49:23.050
a baby poster.

1197
00:49:23.210 --> 00:49:23.370
Yeah.

1198
00:49:23.550 --> 00:49:25.630
But you've got to stay sad.

1199
00:49:25.830 --> 00:49:26.250
Yes.

1200
00:49:26.530 --> 00:49:27.150
It's hard.

1201
00:49:27.350 --> 00:49:27.990
It's really hard.

1202
00:49:28.110 --> 00:49:28.630
That is very difficult.

1203
00:49:29.090 --> 00:49:30.310
Well, here's the thing.

1204
00:49:30.550 --> 00:49:32.450
Michael just gets progressively meaner.

1205
00:49:32.590 --> 00:49:35.230
You know, he calls Meredith a sucker.

1206
00:49:35.470 --> 00:49:37.870
And then Dwight, you know, he opens the paintball.

1207
00:49:37.870 --> 00:49:41.370
And he's like, ugh, you know, how is this better than an iPod?

1208
00:49:41.370 --> 00:49:46.150
And this moment kind of broke my heart, too, when Dwight goes, I never said it was better.

1209
00:49:46.370 --> 00:49:46.910
You know?

1210
00:49:47.590 --> 00:49:47.990
Wait.

1211
00:49:47.990 --> 00:49:50.310
I have an Angela pissed off in this moment.

1212
00:49:50.450 --> 00:49:50.870
Oh, okay.

1213
00:49:50.870 --> 00:49:51.130
Go.

1214
00:49:51.130 --> 00:49:55.530
At 13 minutes, 58 seconds, look at my face.

1215
00:49:55.730 --> 00:49:57.050
I wrote it in all caps.

1216
00:49:57.350 --> 00:50:03.450
So, Michael has just called Meredith a sucker because she got the lame, you know, oven mitt.

1217
00:50:03.650 --> 00:50:04.990
And Phyllis storms out.

1218
00:50:05.410 --> 00:50:05.770
Okay?

1219
00:50:06.010 --> 00:50:06.250
Yeah.

1220
00:50:06.250 --> 00:50:07.810
She is completely heartbroken now.

1221
00:50:07.910 --> 00:50:09.690
And the party is falling apart.

1222
00:50:09.830 --> 00:50:10.070
Mm-hmm.

1223
00:50:10.070 --> 00:50:14.990
And the look on my face is just sheer in, like, rage.

1224
00:50:15.370 --> 00:50:17.430
Now, are we at the top of your rage now?

1225
00:50:17.610 --> 00:50:18.090
No.

1226
00:50:18.090 --> 00:50:18.710
Oh, no.

1227
00:50:18.890 --> 00:50:21.270
Well, I mean, I know we've still got the parking lot, but.

1228
00:50:21.350 --> 00:50:21.670
No.

1229
00:50:21.890 --> 00:50:22.270
Oh, no.

1230
00:50:22.450 --> 00:50:24.410
There's a moment coming, and you'll know it.

1231
00:50:24.630 --> 00:50:29.590
It's the, there's a one-two punch coming at the end for my anger.

1232
00:50:29.910 --> 00:50:30.590
But, yeah.

1233
00:50:30.910 --> 00:50:31.210
All right.

1234
00:50:31.290 --> 00:50:34.670
So, people are making trades, and feelings are getting hurt.

1235
00:50:34.870 --> 00:50:35.150
Yeah.

1236
00:50:35.430 --> 00:50:38.870
And Pam does not go back and get the teapot.

1237
00:50:39.010 --> 00:50:39.970
She gets the iPod.

1238
00:50:40.110 --> 00:50:40.630
She does.

1239
00:50:40.630 --> 00:50:45.370
When it's Pam's turn to pick again, she picks the iPod instead of the teapot.

1240
00:50:45.490 --> 00:50:47.090
And Jim is so hurt.

1241
00:50:47.090 --> 00:50:48.110
He's so hurt.

1242
00:50:48.290 --> 00:50:50.910
And I, you know, I watched this, and I was like, come on, Pam.

1243
00:50:51.050 --> 00:50:55.230
But then, you know, Pam doesn't know what all is in the teapot.

1244
00:50:55.350 --> 00:50:55.910
She doesn't.

1245
00:50:56.010 --> 00:50:57.710
And that's what sort of justified it for me.

1246
00:50:57.770 --> 00:50:59.170
She's just like, this is an iPod.

1247
00:50:59.290 --> 00:51:05.110
This iPod has completely hijacked this whole fun party and gift exchange.

1248
00:51:05.170 --> 00:51:09.430
Because everybody who's sitting in this seat is just thinking about trying to get this iPod.

1249
00:51:09.610 --> 00:51:10.770
And so is Pam.

1250
00:51:11.210 --> 00:51:14.530
Unfortunately, I think she kind of forgot about the teapot.

1251
00:51:14.550 --> 00:51:15.670
So, it was her time to pick.

1252
00:51:15.670 --> 00:51:16.690
She was just like, iPod.

1253
00:51:16.850 --> 00:51:18.910
But she also doesn't know what's in the teapot.

1254
00:51:18.910 --> 00:51:19.450
She doesn't.

1255
00:51:19.470 --> 00:51:21.190
She doesn't know how high the stakes are for Jim.

1256
00:51:21.350 --> 00:51:21.450
No.

1257
00:51:21.570 --> 00:51:22.070
She doesn't.

1258
00:51:22.130 --> 00:51:24.290
I think it's kind of an innocent moment, honestly.

1259
00:51:24.890 --> 00:51:29.730
And Michael has ruined all of this because the gifts were specific for people.

1260
00:51:29.910 --> 00:51:31.930
I mean, Ryan gets a placard that says Kelly.

1261
00:51:32.090 --> 00:51:32.230
Yeah.

1262
00:51:32.330 --> 00:51:34.710
He gets like, you know, a desk, whatever, nameplate.

1263
00:51:34.930 --> 00:51:35.050
Yeah.

1264
00:51:35.130 --> 00:51:38.730
Like, these were not meant to be Yankee swap gifts.

1265
00:51:38.790 --> 00:51:39.350
They were not.

1266
00:51:39.350 --> 00:51:41.150
They were meant for certain people.

1267
00:51:42.130 --> 00:51:45.730
Well, at this point, the party has completely broken down.

1268
00:51:46.090 --> 00:51:48.310
And Michael goes to the liquor store.

1269
00:51:48.590 --> 00:51:50.110
Now, I want to point out a few things.

1270
00:51:50.270 --> 00:51:51.810
I know what you're going to point out.

1271
00:51:52.010 --> 00:51:55.190
Because, lady, I have the DVDs now.

1272
00:51:55.510 --> 00:51:56.350
So, go.

1273
00:51:56.450 --> 00:51:56.850
Do it.

1274
00:51:56.970 --> 00:51:58.050
Do you know what I'm going to say?

1275
00:51:58.230 --> 00:52:00.430
Is it about the attendant at the liquor store?

1276
00:52:00.650 --> 00:52:02.230
I have one thing to say about him.

1277
00:52:02.230 --> 00:52:07.490
But I just thought I wanted to point out that it's also snowing outside the window of the liquor store.

1278
00:52:07.970 --> 00:52:09.590
They made it snow there, too.

1279
00:52:09.850 --> 00:52:10.490
I don't know.

1280
00:52:10.630 --> 00:52:11.190
Nice detail.

1281
00:52:11.390 --> 00:52:11.850
Nice touch.

1282
00:52:12.070 --> 00:52:12.670
Good continuity.

1283
00:52:12.890 --> 00:52:13.510
Veda was on it.

1284
00:52:13.750 --> 00:52:20.070
Well, I read that our writers found out in Pennsylvania that if you work at a liquor store, you have to wear a tie.

1285
00:52:20.210 --> 00:52:20.610
Yes.

1286
00:52:20.890 --> 00:52:25.550
And so, that was part of this character description is that he had to have on a tie.

1287
00:52:25.750 --> 00:52:26.330
Isn't that great?

1288
00:52:26.530 --> 00:52:30.570
And I thought the actor, his name is Ryan Martin, did a fantastic job.

1289
00:52:30.570 --> 00:52:33.410
He just really, like, takes in all of that vodka.

1290
00:52:34.190 --> 00:52:35.150
15 bottles.

1291
00:52:35.230 --> 00:52:35.950
15 bottles.

1292
00:52:37.130 --> 00:52:37.610
Craziness.

1293
00:52:38.370 --> 00:52:40.250
Okay, so then we go back to the party.

1294
00:52:40.430 --> 00:52:49.130
Michael brings all this vodka back into the party, and at 16, 10 minutes, this is the next phase of Angela's spiral.

1295
00:52:49.270 --> 00:52:50.030
Oh, say it.

1296
00:52:50.090 --> 00:52:53.290
So, Michael has vodka, and she's like, what are you doing?

1297
00:52:53.790 --> 00:52:55.870
There's no alcohol at the party.

1298
00:52:56.290 --> 00:52:59.190
You know, Angela speaks up, and Toby speaks up.

1299
00:52:59.330 --> 00:53:00.230
No one else cares.

1300
00:53:00.750 --> 00:53:01.950
But now she's like—

1301
00:53:01.950 --> 00:53:02.510
Toby speaks up?

1302
00:53:02.550 --> 00:53:03.090
I miss that.

1303
00:53:03.250 --> 00:53:06.230
Yeah, Toby's like, Michael, we really shouldn't have it.

1304
00:53:06.230 --> 00:53:07.670
And he goes, just shut it, Toby.

1305
00:53:07.850 --> 00:53:08.590
It's a party.

1306
00:53:08.810 --> 00:53:12.650
But then later, I feel like Toby brings Todd Packer a drink.

1307
00:53:12.870 --> 00:53:13.490
Well, no.

1308
00:53:13.630 --> 00:53:14.390
It's all—

1309
00:53:14.810 --> 00:53:16.450
All bets are off at this point.

1310
00:53:16.450 --> 00:53:26.450
And, you know, you have to remember that Michael told the party planning committee that he wanted this Christmas party to be like, and I quote, a Playboy mansion party.

1311
00:53:26.670 --> 00:53:26.850
Yeah.

1312
00:53:27.110 --> 00:53:28.110
That was his hope.

1313
00:53:28.170 --> 00:53:28.670
That's his goal.

1314
00:53:28.830 --> 00:53:29.670
That's his goal.

1315
00:53:29.670 --> 00:53:33.330
So, but yeah, Angela is now super ticked, because now there's alcohol.

1316
00:53:33.830 --> 00:53:36.110
I'm surprised her whole head didn't explode.

1317
00:53:36.290 --> 00:53:40.210
Well, it's about to, because the next two are what set it into motion.

1318
00:54:08.790 --> 00:54:10.190
Oh, boy.

1319
00:54:10.190 --> 00:54:12.050
Just a quote across it.

1320
00:54:12.130 --> 00:54:12.310
Yeah.

1321
00:54:12.510 --> 00:54:17.910
So, I had a friend at the time who had a t-shirt press, because she had a small business.

1322
00:54:18.330 --> 00:54:21.330
And I loved this line so much.

1323
00:54:21.330 --> 00:54:22.690
I thought it was hilarious.

1324
00:54:22.690 --> 00:54:26.510
Of all people, for Dwight to quote, it would be Billy Zane.

1325
00:54:26.750 --> 00:54:29.130
Well, people were asking if we gave each other gifts.

1326
00:54:29.270 --> 00:54:29.890
That was a gift.

1327
00:54:29.970 --> 00:54:30.510
You gave that out.

1328
00:54:30.570 --> 00:54:32.610
I think you actually gave that out at Christmas that year.

1329
00:54:32.730 --> 00:54:33.050
I did.

1330
00:54:33.050 --> 00:54:34.430
And you gave everyone an ornament.

1331
00:54:34.690 --> 00:54:34.970
Yes.

1332
00:54:34.970 --> 00:54:38.850
I got that cast photo, and I had it printed on an ornament for everyone.

1333
00:54:39.150 --> 00:54:39.330
Yep.

1334
00:54:39.910 --> 00:54:40.150
Aw.

1335
00:54:40.390 --> 00:54:49.790
The idea that Dwight wants to keep the teapot in order to wash out his nasal passages with green tea is based on something that Greg Daniels has actually done.

1336
00:54:50.230 --> 00:54:51.450
Like with a neti pot?

1337
00:54:51.450 --> 00:54:55.470
Yeah, I mean, but I've never put green tea in a neti pot.

1338
00:54:55.850 --> 00:54:56.830
I haven't either.

1339
00:54:56.830 --> 00:54:59.410
I've only used the saline solution that is recommended.

1340
00:54:59.710 --> 00:55:02.790
But I could see Greg reading about it and giving it a try.

1341
00:55:02.970 --> 00:55:03.170
Yeah.

1342
00:55:03.670 --> 00:55:13.050
But Rain, the way Rain was in that scene, and he like shoved that teapot into his nostril.

1343
00:55:13.330 --> 00:55:13.550
Yeah.

1344
00:55:13.930 --> 00:55:18.010
And just John's face as Jim is just like, are you kidding me?

1345
00:55:19.010 --> 00:55:20.890
That's who gets my teapot?

1346
00:55:20.890 --> 00:55:22.370
Like, it's so perfect.

1347
00:55:22.610 --> 00:55:23.670
He's so bummed.

1348
00:55:24.010 --> 00:55:35.830
Now, when I watched this with Lee, Lee said he wondered how Dwight didn't find the note in the box or how Dwight didn't open up the teapot.

1349
00:55:35.830 --> 00:55:37.210
I thought of all of those things.

1350
00:55:37.370 --> 00:55:41.150
I thought Dwight now has the cassette and the sauce packet.

1351
00:55:42.210 --> 00:55:42.570
Yeah.

1352
00:55:42.570 --> 00:55:49.570
I mean, so you have to sort of suspend belief, I guess, at that moment that he took those out and just shoved them aside like, hmm, what's this crap?

1353
00:55:49.690 --> 00:55:51.350
And just sort of shoved them aside in the box.

1354
00:55:51.350 --> 00:55:55.050
Well, also, I don't think Jim is trying to get the teapot back for Pam.

1355
00:55:55.270 --> 00:55:58.050
I think he's just trying to get the teapot back for himself.

1356
00:55:58.290 --> 00:55:59.330
He's just going to keep it now.

1357
00:55:59.570 --> 00:56:06.650
That's what I think the motivation is there because Pam is over, you know, up at the desk with Roy looking through her new iPod.

1358
00:56:06.810 --> 00:56:10.430
I think Jim just wants to get it back because I think there's things inside it that are embarrassing.

1359
00:56:10.430 --> 00:56:11.310
Yes, exactly.

1360
00:56:11.590 --> 00:56:14.870
But he's going to trade the keychain and he's just going to take that teapot home now.

1361
00:56:15.070 --> 00:56:18.810
So Pam is up at reception and she's showing Roy her new iPod.

1362
00:56:18.930 --> 00:56:19.810
He's now at the party.

1363
00:56:19.930 --> 00:56:21.210
He wasn't there for Yankee Swap.

1364
00:56:21.370 --> 00:56:25.350
But he's all excited because now he doesn't have to buy it for Pam for Christmas.

1365
00:56:25.490 --> 00:56:28.090
He was going to buy her this iPod, he tells her.

1366
00:56:28.250 --> 00:56:30.810
And now he doesn't have to or he's just going to get her a sweater.

1367
00:56:31.350 --> 00:56:32.030
Thanks, Roy.

1368
00:56:32.290 --> 00:56:35.730
Now the party is like 15 bottles of vodka in.

1369
00:56:35.850 --> 00:56:37.330
Todd Packer has showed up.

1370
00:56:37.390 --> 00:56:37.830
Oh, yeah.

1371
00:56:37.990 --> 00:56:39.030
It's getting crazy.

1372
00:56:40.030 --> 00:56:41.310
Everyone's doing shots.

1373
00:56:41.470 --> 00:56:42.270
Angela's fuming.

1374
00:56:42.470 --> 00:56:47.490
I am fuming, but the icing on the cake of my pissed offness is about to happen.

1375
00:56:47.730 --> 00:56:48.910
Oh, say it.

1376
00:56:49.310 --> 00:56:52.730
Michael shouts to the whole bullpen.

1377
00:56:52.730 --> 00:56:55.010
He says, oh, my gosh.

1378
00:56:55.150 --> 00:56:57.490
Yes, Ryan, the king of the party planning.

1379
00:56:58.070 --> 00:56:58.670
Oh.

1380
00:56:59.050 --> 00:57:02.130
Thank you to Ryan for this awesome party.

1381
00:57:02.330 --> 00:57:05.850
And the camera pans to me and I am livid.

1382
00:57:06.890 --> 00:57:11.070
Ryan, the temp, the king of the party planning committee?

1383
00:57:11.270 --> 00:57:12.230
Are you kidding me?

1384
00:57:12.350 --> 00:57:12.630
Yeah.

1385
00:57:12.990 --> 00:57:14.370
Oh, that's it.

1386
00:57:14.510 --> 00:57:16.130
She is pissed.

1387
00:57:16.410 --> 00:57:17.290
Oh, no.

1388
00:57:17.770 --> 00:57:19.690
And it's only going to get worse.

1389
00:57:19.970 --> 00:57:23.230
That's not even still the worst thing that's happened to Angela.

1390
00:57:23.490 --> 00:57:23.730
Nope.

1391
00:57:23.730 --> 00:57:26.350
I had a headache by the end of this episode.

1392
00:57:26.370 --> 00:57:26.870
You must have.

1393
00:57:26.870 --> 00:57:31.250
You were just scowling and pushing anger out of your temples this whole episode.

1394
00:57:32.590 --> 00:57:36.990
You know when Todd Packer shows up and he has that line, what's up, my nerds?

1395
00:57:37.010 --> 00:57:37.190
Mm-hmm.

1396
00:57:37.370 --> 00:57:38.190
My nerds.

1397
00:57:38.270 --> 00:57:40.330
That was an improv, sort of.

1398
00:57:40.550 --> 00:57:44.070
In the script, what was written was, what's up, nerds?

1399
00:57:45.350 --> 00:57:50.310
And he just gave it that extra special touch of, what's up, my nerds?

1400
00:57:50.310 --> 00:57:50.670
I know.

1401
00:57:50.790 --> 00:57:52.010
Well, that's also Dave Koechner.

1402
00:57:52.150 --> 00:57:56.030
I mean, I think even the line when he's like, Packer, need a drinky.

1403
00:57:56.230 --> 00:57:56.410
Yeah.

1404
00:57:57.070 --> 00:57:59.490
The line was probably like, he was getting me a drink.

1405
00:57:59.610 --> 00:57:59.790
Yeah.

1406
00:58:00.050 --> 00:58:00.350
You know?

1407
00:58:01.210 --> 00:58:03.130
He brought so much to that role.

1408
00:58:03.250 --> 00:58:03.810
It was amazing.

1409
00:58:03.910 --> 00:58:07.270
And well, you know when he has to lay down on the desk and get the silly string on him,

1410
00:58:07.310 --> 00:58:08.210
like when he passes out?

1411
00:58:08.350 --> 00:58:09.490
I remember shooting that.

1412
00:58:09.630 --> 00:58:11.170
He had to lay there forever.

1413
00:58:11.370 --> 00:58:14.670
So he laid down on those desks, which were not comfortable, right?

1414
00:58:14.830 --> 00:58:16.370
And then they silly stringed his head.

1415
00:58:16.370 --> 00:58:20.030
And then we had all these scenes where that's what he's doing.

1416
00:58:20.310 --> 00:58:24.570
Well, if he got up, all the stuff that he was decorated in would have fallen off.

1417
00:58:24.650 --> 00:58:26.430
It would have been impossible to recreate.

1418
00:58:26.430 --> 00:58:29.790
So he had to just lay there, even when we were on a break.

1419
00:58:29.970 --> 00:58:31.230
Even when we were on a break.

1420
00:58:31.230 --> 00:58:32.630
And he was such a trooper.

1421
00:58:32.770 --> 00:58:33.430
Talk about a trooper.

1422
00:58:33.610 --> 00:58:39.790
And I wrote in my MySpace blog that Kate and I, because Kate and I knew Dave from Improv Days.

1423
00:58:39.830 --> 00:58:41.930
We had all done improv shows together.

1424
00:58:42.190 --> 00:58:46.190
That Kate and I walked over and talked to him while he had to lay on his back.

1425
00:58:46.190 --> 00:58:49.670
Oh, and we just sort of like caught up in that it was so fun to see him.

1426
00:58:49.870 --> 00:58:55.990
But I want you guys to know, if you're wondering what Todd Packer looks like at 20 minutes, 19 seconds,

1427
00:58:56.110 --> 00:58:57.290
to really paint a picture here.

1428
00:58:57.350 --> 00:58:57.570
Yeah.

1429
00:58:57.710 --> 00:59:03.350
He's laying on his back kind of across a desk area partition, right in the middle of the room.

1430
00:59:03.570 --> 00:59:07.950
He has blue silly string on his head, Christmas lights around his torso,

1431
00:59:09.210 --> 00:59:14.390
Christmas garland around his torso, Dwight's desk nameplate on his stomach.

1432
00:59:14.890 --> 00:59:21.190
And there's like a red empty solo cup kind of just like in his, like the crook of his arm.

1433
00:59:21.470 --> 00:59:25.390
And he had to lay like that with all those things on top of him.

1434
00:59:25.570 --> 00:59:28.170
He passes out so quickly.

1435
00:59:28.450 --> 00:59:31.730
You have to imagine he showed up already half drunk.

1436
00:59:31.970 --> 00:59:32.850
You know he did.

1437
00:59:32.850 --> 00:59:33.630
You know he did.

1438
00:59:33.730 --> 00:59:34.510
You know he did.

1439
00:59:34.510 --> 00:59:42.650
Okay, guys, so now we have the scene where Pam reveals to Jim that she got her teapot back.

1440
00:59:43.290 --> 00:59:50.210
She trades Dwight the iPod for the teapot, and now she's going to look inside and find all the iteMs.

1441
00:59:50.230 --> 00:59:53.350
And it's very charming and sweet, and she is so delighted.

1442
00:59:53.570 --> 00:59:59.030
But in this moment, Jim secretly steals the note back and puts it in his pocket.

1443
00:59:59.030 --> 01:00:01.430
I know, he lost his courage.

1444
01:00:01.450 --> 01:00:02.390
He did.

1445
01:00:02.650 --> 01:00:09.710
Now, when we reached out to fans to ask them what they wanted to know about the Christmas episode,

1446
01:00:10.150 --> 01:00:17.230
I would say that about 80% of the comments and emails we received were along the lines of,

1447
01:00:17.570 --> 01:00:19.430
what is in the teapot note?

1448
01:00:19.770 --> 01:00:23.190
Because as you know, in this episode, Pam does not read it.

1449
01:00:23.190 --> 01:00:29.990
It is not revealed, but then in season nine, there's a scene where Jim has the documentary film crew

1450
01:00:29.990 --> 01:00:34.850
put together footage of their romance, and he shows it to Pam,

1451
01:00:35.130 --> 01:00:42.410
and Pam sees that there was a note that Jim steals back, and then he hands it to her, and she reads it.

1452
01:00:42.630 --> 01:00:43.730
How brilliant is that?

1453
01:00:43.850 --> 01:00:44.790
And you know who that is?

1454
01:00:44.890 --> 01:00:45.850
That's Greg Daniels.

1455
01:00:45.930 --> 01:00:46.090
Yeah.

1456
01:00:46.350 --> 01:00:50.470
Because he was such a master at beautiful callback moments.

1457
01:00:51.050 --> 01:00:52.250
I love that.

1458
01:00:52.250 --> 01:00:56.070
Well, from the time that Jim stole the note, it drove people crazy.

1459
01:00:56.410 --> 01:00:59.630
They always wanted to know what had been written in the note.

1460
01:00:59.790 --> 01:01:01.290
Would Pam ever get the note?

1461
01:01:01.430 --> 01:01:04.150
For years and years, will he ever give her the note?

1462
01:01:04.450 --> 01:01:07.910
Around the time of the wedding, people wanted him to give it to her as a wedding gift.

1463
01:01:08.590 --> 01:01:10.210
Greg saved it till the end.

1464
01:01:11.190 --> 01:01:13.690
I'm going to say something that I've never said before.

1465
01:01:13.690 --> 01:01:15.970
I also feel like I'm maybe going to cry.

1466
01:01:16.470 --> 01:01:16.950
What?

1467
01:01:17.190 --> 01:01:17.670
Wait.

1468
01:01:18.190 --> 01:01:18.670
Wait.

1469
01:01:18.970 --> 01:01:19.350
What?

1470
01:01:20.030 --> 01:01:22.890
Are you going to say what was in the note?

1471
01:01:23.470 --> 01:01:25.090
Are you going to say what was in the note?

1472
01:01:26.450 --> 01:01:27.190
Sort of.

1473
01:01:27.670 --> 01:01:30.150
Because I don't know what was on that card.

1474
01:01:30.390 --> 01:01:31.230
None of us do.

1475
01:01:31.750 --> 01:01:34.210
I'm the only one who knows, and John knows.

1476
01:01:34.710 --> 01:01:36.230
Oh my gosh, lady.

1477
01:01:36.230 --> 01:01:54.650
In that episode in Season 9, I believe Greg suggested to John that he write a personal message from himself to me, just saying what our time together on The Office meant to him.

1478
01:01:54.750 --> 01:01:55.510
Oh, Jenna.

1479
01:01:56.890 --> 01:01:58.590
Because we were wrapping up filming.

1480
01:01:58.770 --> 01:02:02.510
We were wrapping up the series, and we were all so emotional at that time, you know?

1481
01:02:02.850 --> 01:02:06.130
It was all, we were all sort of saying goodbye in different ways.

1482
01:02:06.390 --> 01:02:06.610
We were.

1483
01:02:06.870 --> 01:02:09.890
And so, that was his goodbye.

1484
01:02:11.090 --> 01:02:22.330
Very similar to when we filmed that scene with Steve, where I said goodbye to him at the airport, and Paul Feig told me, just run up and say goodbye to your friend Steve.

1485
01:02:23.130 --> 01:02:30.170
Jeff Blitz said the same thing to me when I was in the car with Oscar, and I say I love Dwight.

1486
01:02:30.730 --> 01:02:39.570
He said, Angela, in this moment, express your love for the show and everyone, and if you couldn't have it in your life anymore.

1487
01:02:40.630 --> 01:02:42.030
And I disintegrated.

1488
01:02:42.330 --> 01:02:42.470
Yeah.

1489
01:02:43.370 --> 01:02:50.530
So, I'm on camera, and I open up this note that John's written me, and I just start crying.

1490
01:02:50.810 --> 01:02:51.990
I just start bawling.

1491
01:02:52.230 --> 01:02:54.330
It probably, the first take was probably not usable.

1492
01:02:56.690 --> 01:02:58.170
It was the sweetest note.

1493
01:02:58.170 --> 01:03:05.390
And, you know, on camera, Pam says, I'll never say what it said, but just know it was perfect.

1494
01:03:06.790 --> 01:03:12.070
Well, I'll never say exactly what John wrote, but I will say just know it was perfect.

1495
01:03:13.490 --> 01:03:15.510
So, that's what was in the teapot note, guys.

1496
01:03:15.670 --> 01:03:17.770
It was a note from John to me.

1497
01:03:17.930 --> 01:03:21.410
A personal note about what it meant to work with you on the show.

1498
01:03:21.530 --> 01:03:21.770
Yeah.

1499
01:03:21.990 --> 01:03:22.290
Yeah.

1500
01:03:22.410 --> 01:03:24.270
About our time together on the show, and it was really sweet.

1501
01:03:24.470 --> 01:03:27.210
Well, that would completely wreck me.

1502
01:03:27.510 --> 01:03:27.890
Yeah.

1503
01:03:28.450 --> 01:03:29.990
Oh, I love that.

1504
01:03:30.170 --> 01:03:31.110
I didn't know that.

1505
01:03:31.230 --> 01:03:31.770
Are you okay?

1506
01:03:32.110 --> 01:03:32.590
Yeah.

1507
01:03:32.810 --> 01:03:33.250
Well, crap.

1508
01:03:33.250 --> 01:03:34.710
