1556
01:05:12.330 --> 01:05:16.190
You have a guy up on the roof, and he's got the soap snow.

1557
01:05:16.190 --> 01:05:16.750
Yep.

1558
01:05:16.950 --> 01:05:17.510
That he's going to-

1559
01:05:17.510 --> 01:05:18.470
Falling into your eyes.

1560
01:05:18.550 --> 01:05:19.090
He's going to-

1561
01:05:19.090 --> 01:05:19.210
Yeah.

1562
01:05:19.970 --> 01:05:20.370
Stinging.

1563
01:05:21.290 --> 01:05:24.950
And then there's snow on the ground, because they've put real snow on the ground.

1564
01:05:24.950 --> 01:05:28.090
We filmed this scene at the end of the day, and everyone had gone.

1565
01:05:28.550 --> 01:05:32.510
It was just me and Charles McDougall, Randall Einhorn, and Mike Schur.

1566
01:05:32.630 --> 01:05:34.710
So, it was just a kind of a skeleton crew at this point.

1567
01:05:34.710 --> 01:05:36.670
Those are always some of my most favorite shoots.

1568
01:05:36.970 --> 01:05:37.850
Yeah, me too.

1569
01:05:37.970 --> 01:05:39.910
And we did not have a lot of time.

1570
01:05:40.330 --> 01:05:41.810
We didn't have a lot of time to get this.

1571
01:05:41.930 --> 01:05:42.630
Oh, the clock was ticking.

1572
01:05:42.910 --> 01:05:43.630
Yeah, exactly.

1573
01:05:43.710 --> 01:05:47.450
Because we didn't want to go into overtime for everyone, and it was the end of the day.

1574
01:05:47.770 --> 01:05:51.650
And so, Charles McDougall said to me, we're probably only going to do like two takes,

1575
01:05:52.330 --> 01:05:53.870
you know, maybe three.

1576
01:05:53.870 --> 01:06:01.530
