Watch the scene.

1589
01:06:21.390 --> 01:06:21.970
I throw them down.

1590
01:06:21.970 --> 01:06:24.270
They bounce straight up in the air.

1591
01:06:24.410 --> 01:06:25.210
What were they?

1592
01:06:25.390 --> 01:06:28.230
They were like some kind of plastic composite whatever.

1593
01:06:28.610 --> 01:06:29.250
Oh, no.

1594
01:06:29.570 --> 01:06:31.410
So, when you look, watch it, you guys.

1595
01:06:31.530 --> 01:06:33.010
You see them bounce in the air.

1596
01:06:33.390 --> 01:06:35.730
I assumed, well, that makes sense.

1597
01:06:35.730 --> 01:06:41.230
We did not have the budget to get special breakaway glass ornaments, and there's no way

1598
01:06:41.230 --> 01:06:42.670
they would give you real glass.

1599
01:06:42.870 --> 01:06:43.250
No.

1600
01:06:43.450 --> 01:06:46.470
So, these things bounced like a tennis ball.

1601
01:06:46.750 --> 01:06:48.830
And so, Charles is like, cut.

1602
01:06:48.930 --> 01:06:50.570
And he goes, okay, two things.

1603
01:06:50.570 --> 01:06:53.370
One, we need you to stand closer to the wall.

1604
01:06:53.510 --> 01:06:56.890
Like, if you can in the scene, get as close to the wall as possible, because that's where

1605
01:06:56.890 --> 01:06:59.450
the guy is with the soap coming down.

1606
01:06:59.650 --> 01:06:59.830
Yeah.

1607
01:06:59.830 --> 01:07:01.350
The soap doesn't ball very far.

1608
01:07:01.550 --> 01:07:01.770
Yeah.

1609
01:07:02.010 --> 01:07:03.250
So, we have another take.

1610
01:07:03.750 --> 01:07:05.570
And he's like, why aren't you breaking the ornaments?

1611
01:07:05.710 --> 01:07:06.710
I'm like, Charles, they're bouncing.

1612
01:07:06.710 --> 01:07:07.530
What are you talking about?

1613
01:07:07.690 --> 01:07:08.790
He goes, can you throw them harder?

1614
01:07:08.930 --> 01:07:10.590
I was like, yeah, they're just going to bounce higher.

1615
01:07:10.830 --> 01:07:11.150
Oh.

1616
01:07:11.390 --> 01:07:13.050
And I was like, okay, I got it.

1617
01:07:13.090 --> 01:07:13.410
I got it.

1618
01:07:13.430 --> 01:07:14.010
I have an idea.

1619
01:07:20.570 --> 01:07:25.590
Again, the most awesome photo that I have, and it's the snow falling and me throwing

1620
01:07:25.590 --> 01:07:29.210
the ornaments and Charles McDougal in the distance watching me.

1621
01:07:29.530 --> 01:07:29.930
Oh.

1622
01:07:30.290 --> 01:07:30.490
It's the cooleSt.

1623
01:07:30.490 --> 01:07:30.910
That's great.

1624
01:07:31.030 --> 01:07:32.770
Michael Gallenberg, our set designer.

1625
01:07:32.890 --> 01:07:33.110
Yeah.

1626
01:07:33.110 --> 01:07:33.970
He took this photo.

1627
01:07:34.090 --> 01:07:34.610
It was so cool.

1628
01:07:34.750 --> 01:07:36.070
But anyway, here I am.

1629
01:07:36.270 --> 01:07:37.170
We're running out of time.

1630
01:07:37.390 --> 01:07:38.110
I got to stand.

1631
01:07:38.230 --> 01:07:39.490
I got to get myself to the wall.

1632
01:07:39.650 --> 01:07:42.090
I got to throw these ornaments, and I need them to break.

1633
01:07:42.390 --> 01:07:44.090
And I have to shriek, right?

1634
01:07:44.570 --> 01:07:47.430
So I throw them with, I said, I'm going to throw them harder this time.

1635
01:07:47.430 --> 01:07:47.870
I don't know.

1636
01:07:48.010 --> 01:07:49.490
So I threw them as hard as I could.

1637
01:07:50.090 --> 01:07:51.310
They bounced up higher.

1638
01:07:52.150 --> 01:07:57.170
I shrieked, and I just started stomping on them and shattering them with my feet.

1639
01:07:57.290 --> 01:08:00.650
Was that your intention going in when you're like, I have an idea.

1640
01:08:00.650 --> 01:08:01.170
I can do it.

1641
01:08:01.210 --> 01:08:01.490
I can do it.

1642
01:08:01.490 --> 01:08:04.770
I was thinking, if I can't get them to break, I have to start stomping on them.

1643
01:08:04.810 --> 01:08:05.130
Yes.

1644
01:08:05.250 --> 01:08:06.390
So that's what I just did.

1645
01:08:06.510 --> 01:08:07.690
That was just an improv in the moment.

1646
01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:08.910
I just started stomping on them.

1647
01:08:09.310 --> 01:08:11.470
Folks, notice I'm wearing my Sass shoes.

1648
01:08:11.770 --> 01:08:13.870
Oh, that's the perfect shoe for this.

1649
01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:14.630
I know.

1650
01:08:14.830 --> 01:08:15.970
And so I shriek.

1651
01:08:16.090 --> 01:08:16.930
I get to the wall.

1652
01:08:17.090 --> 01:08:17.990
I'm stomping things.

1653
01:08:18.090 --> 01:08:19.350
I rip the box apart.

1654
01:08:19.850 --> 01:08:20.990
We got the scene.

1655
01:08:21.570 --> 01:08:21.850
Oh.

1656
01:08:22.350 --> 01:08:27.750
Let me tell you, ToneLoke89 is going to be very happy because they wrote in with a fan question.

1657
01:08:27.950 --> 01:08:28.590
