Even if I had to, like, be in a bathing suit, I'd feel awkward.

1762
01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:37.250
You know what I mean?

1763
01:12:37.350 --> 01:12:38.610
Kate was wearing pasties.

1764
01:12:38.770 --> 01:12:39.570
Kate had things.

1765
01:12:39.570 --> 01:12:40.590
She was kind of covered.

1766
01:12:40.730 --> 01:12:40.830
Yeah.

1767
01:12:40.950 --> 01:12:42.570
She had things over her hoo-hahs.

1768
01:12:42.750 --> 01:12:42.890
Yeah.

1769
01:12:43.150 --> 01:12:44.290
Steve is such a gentleman.

1770
01:12:44.490 --> 01:12:46.470
He said, Kate, I'm just going to look at, like, your neck.

1771
01:12:46.730 --> 01:12:47.030
Yeah.

1772
01:12:47.690 --> 01:12:48.890
Stare at your clavicle.

1773
01:12:49.110 --> 01:12:50.950
They had no crew inside.

1774
01:12:51.230 --> 01:12:51.350
Yep.

1775
01:12:51.490 --> 01:12:53.830
Her image wasn't on any monitors anywhere.

1776
01:12:53.830 --> 01:12:54.610
That's right.

1777
01:12:54.830 --> 01:12:57.230
And there was no chip in the digital camera.

1778
01:12:57.490 --> 01:12:59.010
So the flash goes off.

1779
01:12:59.090 --> 01:13:03.030
It looks like Michael's taking a picture, but there was actually never a picture taken.

1780
01:13:03.310 --> 01:13:03.670
Never a photo.

1781
01:13:03.850 --> 01:13:09.010
So they were very, very mindful of taking care of Kate in that moment.

1782
01:13:09.510 --> 01:13:13.510
Kate would go on as Meredith to take off her clothes.

1783
01:13:13.930 --> 01:13:14.550
Quite a bit.

1784
01:13:14.650 --> 01:13:15.110
Quite a bit.

1785
01:13:15.110 --> 01:13:20.830
But one of my favorite things is that Kate's father wrote her a handwritten letter.

1786
01:13:21.050 --> 01:13:22.010
Oh, my goodness.

1787
01:13:22.430 --> 01:13:26.910
And all it said, this is her father, who, you know, Kate is from Pennsylvania.

1788
01:13:27.170 --> 01:13:32.550
And all it said was, dear Kate, stop taking your clothes off.

1789
01:13:33.030 --> 01:13:33.770
Love, Dad.

1790
01:13:33.770 --> 01:13:35.210
Oh, my gosh.

1791
01:13:36.410 --> 01:13:37.650
Oh, my gosh.

1792
01:13:38.590 --> 01:13:40.170
What did Kate do?

1793
01:13:40.330 --> 01:13:41.590
How did she respond to that?

1794
01:13:41.830 --> 01:13:42.850
She was like, oh, man.

1795
01:13:43.290 --> 01:13:45.770
Now, is that her dad having a sense of humor?

1796
01:13:45.770 --> 01:13:48.350
Or is that him being like, seriously, stop it?

1797
01:13:48.530 --> 01:13:49.270
I think both.

1798
01:13:49.450 --> 01:13:50.010
I think both.

1799
01:13:50.210 --> 01:13:50.510
All right.

1800
01:13:50.610 --> 01:13:52.170
Should we talk about the parking lot?

1801
01:13:52.310 --> 01:13:53.810
We're almost done here.

1802
01:13:54.350 --> 01:13:54.790
Yes.

1803
01:13:54.930 --> 01:13:56.110
Let's talk about the parking lot.

1804
01:13:56.250 --> 01:14:02.190
Because it is definitely one of the most magical moments that I remember in filming all nine years.

1805
01:14:02.190 --> 01:14:03.570
And we all say that.

1806
01:14:03.770 --> 01:14:04.050
Yeah.

1807
01:14:04.230 --> 01:14:07.650
People often ask, like, what were your favorite scenes?

1808
01:14:07.930 --> 01:14:14.390
And it's always hard to explain because sometimes your favorite scene, it doesn't seem like that exciting of a scene.

1809
01:14:14.530 --> 01:14:17.890
But it's what happened behind the scenes that make it your favorite.

1810
01:14:18.010 --> 01:14:19.770
And this parking lot scene is one of mine.

1811
01:14:20.350 --> 01:14:20.790
Definitely.

1812
01:14:21.310 --> 01:14:21.570
Definitely.

1813
01:14:22.050 --> 01:14:22.350
Okay.

1814
01:14:22.370 --> 01:14:23.970
So it's the end of the day.

1815
01:14:23.970 --> 01:14:26.370
We have all of this real snow on the ground.

1816
01:14:26.690 --> 01:14:28.270
And everyone is leaving.

1817
01:14:28.270 --> 01:14:29.890
And everyone's in good spirits.

1818
01:14:30.190 --> 01:14:31.410
And it's really nighttime.

1819
01:14:31.410 --> 01:14:34.170
It was rare for us to ever work past 6 p.m.

1820
01:14:34.190 --> 01:14:35.430
So we always got excited.

1821
01:14:35.790 --> 01:14:40.170
To walk out in the dark, I think, we all felt like we were up past our bedtime.

1822
01:14:40.430 --> 01:14:42.910
But also, you have to remember, this is Los Angeles.

1823
01:14:43.170 --> 01:14:45.030
There's never snow on the ground.

1824
01:14:45.030 --> 01:14:50.270
So this is magical in itself that we have a parking lot full of snow.

1825
01:14:50.650 --> 01:14:58.950
And as we're walking to the cars, I don't know, like, the shot you see, I'm actually in the front passenger seat of an SUV.

1826
01:14:59.170 --> 01:15:01.270
But I'm only half in, like, the door's open.

1827
01:15:01.270 --> 01:15:05.950
But I remember one of the guys just picked up some snow and flung it at the other one.

1828
01:15:06.170 --> 01:15:11.310
And then they all started picking up snow and having this impromptu snowball fight.

1829
01:15:11.410 --> 01:15:11.590
Yeah.

1830
01:15:11.890 --> 01:15:13.310
And everyone loved it.

1831
01:15:13.390 --> 01:15:14.890
And they wanted us to keep doing it.

1832
01:15:15.010 --> 01:15:19.650
But it was just sort of like us just all hanging out in the snow.

1833
01:15:19.970 --> 01:15:20.170
Yeah.

1834
01:15:20.350 --> 01:15:22.350
And we turned into a bunch of kids.

1835
01:15:22.570 --> 01:15:22.950
We did.

1836
01:15:23.210 --> 01:15:23.550
We couldn't help it.

1837
01:15:23.670 --> 01:15:23.930
Yeah.

1838
01:15:23.930 --> 01:15:27.250
We were up past our bedtime with snow on the ground.

1839
01:15:27.630 --> 01:15:28.710
Fresh snow on the ground.

1840
01:15:29.030 --> 01:15:30.210
It was so fun.

1841
01:15:30.370 --> 01:15:37.050
And, you know, I have a picture of all of us together in the parking lot with Charles McDougal.

1842
01:15:37.510 --> 01:15:38.850
And it's great.

1843
01:15:38.850 --> 01:15:39.730
I love it.

1844
01:15:39.770 --> 01:15:40.630
I covet it.

1845
01:15:40.810 --> 01:15:41.750
I covet it.

1846
01:15:41.750 --> 01:15:41.890
I love that.

1847
01:15:41.970 --> 01:15:42.790
I want to see it.

1848
01:15:42.930 --> 01:15:43.190
Yeah.

1849
01:15:43.470 --> 01:15:46.830
Well, this is why we have to make our scrapbook thingy, Angela.

1850
01:15:47.070 --> 01:15:47.430
We do.

1851
01:15:47.470 --> 01:15:48.190
We should combine.

1852
01:15:48.370 --> 01:15:49.410
Well, that's what we need to do.

1853
01:15:49.490 --> 01:15:52.810
We need to compile and combine all of our stuff.

1854
01:15:53.210 --> 01:15:56.450
And then make it so that we can both have what we both have.

1855
01:15:56.970 --> 01:15:57.370
Yeah.

1856
01:15:57.790 --> 01:15:58.130
Right?

1857
01:15:58.410 --> 01:15:58.650
Yeah.

1858
01:15:58.930 --> 01:15:59.110
Yeah.

1859
01:15:59.290 --> 01:16:01.530
Before we lose it all, we need to do it.

1860
01:16:02.130 --> 01:16:02.530
Okay.

1861
01:16:02.750 --> 01:16:03.530
It's 2020.

1862
01:16:04.810 --> 01:16:06.090
We need to do this.

1863
01:16:06.190 --> 01:16:07.290
This is a goal for this year.

1864
01:16:07.370 --> 01:16:09.130
I'm setting the goal for us this year.

1865
01:16:09.290 --> 01:16:10.890
Well, you guys, she said it.

1866
01:16:11.150 --> 01:16:13.990
Now I've got to, like, Jenna's going to put me to task.

1867
01:16:14.170 --> 01:16:15.650
This episode was really special.

1868
01:16:15.730 --> 01:16:16.090
It was.

1869
01:16:16.290 --> 01:16:19.810
I really hope we did it justice because it means so much to us.

1870
01:16:19.810 --> 01:16:25.090
These episodes are almost harder for me than other ones because there's so much emotion

1871
01:16:25.090 --> 01:16:25.930
attached to it.

1872
01:16:26.070 --> 01:16:27.870
There's so much that happens in the scene.

1873
01:16:28.330 --> 01:16:33.290
Not only, like, is it special to us personally, but it was, like, a big moment for our characters.

1874
01:16:33.570 --> 01:16:33.770
Yeah.

1875
01:16:34.010 --> 01:16:40.990
And just that moment at the end, that snowball fight, that is just a group of people who love

1876
01:16:40.990 --> 01:16:43.350
each other, who are all getting to hang out.

1877
01:16:43.590 --> 01:16:43.950
Mm-hmm.

1878
01:16:43.990 --> 01:16:45.950
And we just happen to be on a TV show together.

1879
01:16:46.370 --> 01:16:46.450
Yeah.

1880
01:16:46.450 --> 01:16:50.570
It's just a really special moment, and I love that they let that be how it ended.

1881
01:16:50.910 --> 01:16:56.250
And that's really how it felt when we left this show, that we were just a bunch of friends

1882
01:16:56.250 --> 01:17:01.650
who happened to be on a TV show together because we were friends.

1883
01:17:01.850 --> 01:17:02.990
And we are friends.

1884
01:17:03.110 --> 01:17:03.310
Yeah.

1885
01:17:03.670 --> 01:17:04.530
And we're family.

1886
01:17:04.730 --> 01:17:05.170
We are.

1887
01:17:05.550 --> 01:17:09.010
So next week, we've got another big episode, Ange.

1888
01:17:09.270 --> 01:17:09.850
Huge episode.

1889
01:17:09.850 --> 01:17:17.070
I mean, listen, the rest of this season two is just going to be one momentous episode

1890
01:17:17.070 --> 01:17:17.710
after the other.

1891
